{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015yUfhM46jTLMjvQFvUTamd","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/standard-operating-procedures.md b/standard-operating-procedures.md\nindex 0f7bf9f..51559db 100644\n--- a/standard-operating-procedures.md\n+++ b/standard-operating-procedures.md\n@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@ hankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n ├── tests/                  ← unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n ├── schemas/                ← generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n ├── shims/                  ← agent harness adapters\n+├── docs/                   ← documentation site workspace (Next.js + Nextra)\n+│   ├── app/                ← Next.js app directory\n+│   ├── content/            ← MDX documentation pages\n+│   ├── components/         ← custom React components\n+│   ├── public/             ← static assets + generated schemas\n+│   └── package.json        ← hankweave-docs workspace\n ├── learning/               ← example hanks and guides (ships to public)\n ├── intermediates/          ← planning docs, numbered by feature (internal only)\n ├── external-docs/          ← SDK reference docs for agent context (internal only)\n@@ -23,21 +29,23 @@ hankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n ├── .github/                ← CI workflows and composite actions\n ├── CHANGELOG.md            ← Keep a Changelog format, [Unreleased] workflow\n ├── CONTRIBUTING.md         ← branch model and PR guidelines (internal only)\n-└── package.json            ← @southbridgeai/hankweave (private npm)\n+└── package.json            ← @southbridgeai/hankweave (private npm) + workspace root\n ```\n \n+The documentation site (`docs/`) deploys to Vercel from this repo. It is a Bun workspace but does not have a workspace dependency on the runtime package.\n+\n There is a separate public repo at `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` which receives sanitized snapshots via the sync workflow. It publishes the public `hankweave` npm package.\n \n ### What gets stripped before public release\n \n The sync process (`scripts/sync-public.ts`) removes internal-only content:\n \n-- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`\n+- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`, `docs/`\n - **Files**: `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `PUBLISHING-PLAN.md`, `telemetry.md` (root), `reference/telemetry.md` (internal version), `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`, `scripts/sync-public.ts`, `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `.DS_Store`\n \n The `public-release-files/` directory contains replacements that get overlaid: a public-facing `README.md`, `LICENSE.md`, `NOTICE.md`, a sanitized `reference/telemetry.md`, and a simplified `.github/workflows/release.yml`.\n \n-The `package.json` is transformed: name becomes `hankweave`, `publishConfig.access` becomes `public`, `homepage` points to the public repo, and `release:*` scripts are removed.\n+The `package.json` is transformed: name becomes `hankweave`, `publishConfig.access` becomes `public`, `homepage` points to the public repo, `release:*` scripts are removed, and the `workspaces` field is deleted (since docs are not included in the public repo).\n \n ---\n \n@@ -96,6 +104,19 @@ These are stripped from release/alpha and the public repo.\n \n `external-docs/` holds SDK documentation and reference material (Claude Code SDK, AI SDK, Gemini CLI, etc.). These exist primarily so AI agents have context when working on integrations. Stripped before release.\n \n+### Documentation site\n+\n+The documentation site is a Bun workspace at `docs/`. To work on it locally, first ensure dependencies are installed from the repo root (`bun install`), then:\n+\n+    cd docs && bun run dev    # Development server with hot reload (uses --turbopack)\n+    cd docs && bun run build  # Production build\n+\n+Changes to docs pages (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`) deploy automatically via Vercel when pushed to the configured branch.\n+\n+Schema generation writes to both `schemas/` (for the npm package) and `docs/public/schemas/` (for the docs site):\n+\n+    bun run generate-schemas\n+\n ---\n \n ## 4. PR Conventions\n@@ -352,6 +373,8 @@ Rules:\n | `server/config-validation/`            | Validation schemas for hank files and configs                                 |\n | `tests/utils/sentinel-test-harness.ts` | Shared test utilities for sentinel tests                                      |\n | `tests/utils/mock-llm.ts`              | Mock LLM provider for integration tests                                       |\n+| `docs/package.json`                    | Documentation site workspace (hankweave-docs)                                 |\n+| `docs/content/`                        | MDX documentation pages (concepts, guides, reference)                         |\n \n ---","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b4944f-9ed8-419f-b1b0-aa5790b55960","uuid":"abcb9935-41c0-45cc-abed-fb82998f7fce","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/standard-operating-procedures.md b/standard-operating-procedures.md\nindex 0f7bf9f..51559db 100644\n--- a/standard-operating-procedures.md\n+++ b/standard-operating-procedures.md\n@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@ hankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n ├── tests/                  ← unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n ├── schemas/                ← generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n ├── shims/                  ← agent harness adapters\n+├── docs/                   ← documentation site workspace (Next.js + Nextra)\n+│   ├── app/                ← Next.js app directory\n+│   ├── content/            ← MDX documentation pages\n+│   ├── components/         ← custom React components\n+│   ├── public/             ← static assets + generated schemas\n+│   └── package.json        ← hankweave-docs workspace\n ├── learning/          