{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018e85CWn251V8MgmsfRgJFi","type":"tool_result","content":"   104→\n   105→`external-docs/` holds SDK documentation and reference material (Claude Code SDK, AI SDK, Gemini CLI, etc.). These exist primarily so AI agents have context when working on integrations. Stripped before release.\n   106→\n   107→### Documentation site\n   108→\n   109→The documentation site is a Bun workspace at `docs/`. To work on it locally, first ensure dependencies are installed from the repo root (`bun install`), then:\n   110→\n   111→    cd docs && bun run dev    # Development server with hot reload (uses --turbopack)\n   112→    cd docs && bun run build  # Production build\n   113→\n   114→Changes to docs pages (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`) deploy automatically via Vercel when pushed to the configured branch.\n   115→\n   116→Schema generation writes to both `schemas/` (for the npm package) and `docs/public/schemas/` (for the docs site):\n   117→\n   118→    bun run generate-schemas\n   119→\n   120→---\n   121→\n   122→## 4. PR Conventions\n   123→\n   124→### Title format\n   125→\n   126→Include Linear ticket numbers when applicable:\n   127→\n   128→```\n   129→Fixes: Sentinel drains, telemetry fixes, rollback QoL (ENG-194, ENG-193)\n   130→Quality-of-Life Improvements Batch 3 (ENG-158, ENG-180, ENG-179)\n   131→CC not exiting Bug (ENG-186)\n   132→```\n   133→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b4944f-9ed8-419f-b1b0-aa5790b55960","uuid":"7676546f-4387-4005-b582-8bd5e1afd385","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md","content":"\n`external-docs/` holds SDK documentation and reference material (Claude Code SDK, AI SDK, Gemini CLI, etc.). These exist primarily so AI agents have context when working on integrations. Stripped before release.\n\n### Documentation site\n\nThe documentation site is a Bun workspace at `docs/`. To work on it locally, first ensure dependencies are installed from the repo root (`bun install`), then:\n\n    cd docs && bun run dev    # Development server with hot reload (uses --turbopack)\n    cd docs && bun run build  # Production build\n\nChanges to docs pages (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`) deploy automatically via Vercel when pushed to the configured branch.\n\nSchema generation writes to both `schemas/` (for the npm package) and `docs/public/schemas/` (for the docs site):\n\n    bun run generate-schemas\n\n---\n\n## 4. PR Conventions\n\n### Title format\n\nInclude Linear ticket numbers when applicable:\n\n```\nFixes: Sentinel drains, telemetry fixes, rollback QoL (ENG-194, ENG-193)\nQuality-of-Life Improvements Batch 3 (ENG-158, ENG-180, ENG-179)\nCC not exiting Bug (ENG-186)\n```\n","numLines":30,"startLine":104,"totalLines":429}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:58:54.072Z"}
