tatus":"completed","activeForm":"Running bun install"},{"content":"Verify docs build","status":"completed","activeForm":"Verifying docs build"},{"content":"Run full verification (lint, typecheck, tests)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Running full verification"},{"content":"Run schema generation verification","status":"completed","activeForm":"Verifying schema generation"},{"content":"Verify npm pack excludes docs","status":"completed","activeForm":"Verifying npm pack"},{"content":"Run runtime build verification","status":"completed","activeForm":"Running runtime build verification"},{"content":"Cross-check all plan phases against implementation","status":"completed","activeForm":"Cross-checking all plan phases"},{"content":"Update implementation_issues.md with findings","status":"in_progress","activeForm":"Updating implementation issues log"}]},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:59:20.419Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_014AJx6iwpKxu1TcVcmR1MxK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WyT6QJx3oTUfB7tH8nQzjj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/implementations/current/implementation_issues.md","content":"# Implementation Issues and Observations\n\n## Overview\n\nThe implementation was already substantially complete when this agent began its review. All 8 phases from the plan were implemented and verified. This document records what was found, what was confirmed, and what observations might inform plan updates.\n\n---\n\n## State on Agent Start\n\nAll code changes were already in place as uncommitted modifications on the `develop` branch of `source/hankweave/`. The `docs/` directory was present as an untracked directory. The following files showed modifications via `git status`:\n\n- `.gitignore`\n- `bun.lock`\n- `package.json`\n- `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`\n- `scripts/generate-schemas.ts`\n- `scripts/release.ts`\n- `scripts/sync-public.ts`\n- `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`\n- `standard-operating-procedures.md`\n- `tsconfig.json`\n\nThis matched the expected change set from the plan's Summary of Changes table exactly.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Results\n\n### Linting (`bun run lint`)\n\nPassed cleanly. Biome checked 230 files with no fixes required. The changes to the scripts directory (which is excluded from Biome's `includes` per the plan's note in edge case 8) did not cause any issues.\n\n### Typecheck (`bun run tc`)\n\nFailed with the expected pre-existing error:\n\n```\nerror TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for 'bun-types'.\n```\n\nThis is the pre-existing issue documented in the plan (Phase 0, Step 0.2 and Section g). Only this single error was present — no additional errors introduced by the migration. The `docs/**/*` exclusion in `tsconfig.json` is correctly preventing docs TypeScript files from being picked up by the runtime's tsconfig.\n\n### Unit Tests (`bun run test:unit`)\n\nExact expected baseline: **1512 pass, 4 skip, 9 fail**. All 9 failures are the pre-existing Codex binary locator tests. No new failures introduced.\n\n### Integration Tests (`bun test tests/integration`)\n\n**163 pass, 0 fail**. Passed cleanly.\n\n### Schema Generation (`bun run generate-schemas`)\n\nCorrectly wrote to both:\n- `schemas/hank.schema.json`, `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`, `schemas/sentinel.schema.json`\n- `docs/public/schemas/hank.schema.json`, `docs/public/schemas/hankweave.schema.json`, `docs/public/schemas/sentinel.schema.json`\n\n### Runtime Build (`bun run build`)\n\nSucceeded. Output at `dist/index.js` (1799.54 KB minified).\n\n### Docs Build (`cd docs && bun run build`)\n\nSucceeded. Next.js compiled successfully (36 static pages). The `postbuild` Pagefind step also ran and indexed 32 pages.\n\nOne warning from Next.js was observed:\n\n```\nWarning: Next.js inferred your workspace root, but it may not be correct.\nWe detected multiple lockfiles and selected the directory of /Users/philip/package-lock.json as the root directory.\nTo silence this warning, set `outputFileTracingRoot` in your Next.js config, or consider removing one of the lockfiles if it's not needed.\nSee https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/config/next-config-js/output#caveats for more information.\nDetected additional lockfiles:\n  * /Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave/bun.lock\n```\n\nThis is a cosmetic warning from Next.js's workspace root detection heuristic on the agent's local machine — it found a `package-lock.json` higher up in the directory tree (the agent's home directory) and used that instead of the monorepo's `bun.lock`. This is an environment-specific artifact and will not appear in the actual deployment environment. The build still succeeded. **The plan could mention this potential warning in a local dev environment note.** A fix would be to set `outputFileTracingRoot` in `docs/next.config.mjs`, but this is cosmetic and not required.\n\n### npm Pack (`npm pack --dry-run`)\n\nThe tarball contains only `dist/`, `shims/`, `schemas/`, and metadata. `docs/` is correctly absent, confirming the `\"files\"` allowlist in `package.json` prevents docs from being included in the npm package.\n\n### Release Dry-Run (`bun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks`)\n\nThe release script correctly detected uncommitted changes (the migration changes not yet committed) and halted. This is correct behavior — the release script requires a clean working directory. The script showed all migration files in the uncommitted list, which is expected.\n\n---\n\n## Schema Diff Note\n\nThe plan predicted a cosmetic schema diff from unified dependency resolution. The actual schema diff found was:\n\n```diff\n+        \"showCosts\": {\n+          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n+          \"description\": \"If true, display cost data in the TUI\"\n+        },\n```\n\nThis is 4 lines added to `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`, but the change is **not from dependency resolution** — it is from the `philipn/eng-213-hankweave_runtime_show_costs` PR that was merged into `develop` before this migration. The plan's prediction about cosmetic dependency-resolution diffs was not triggered in this environment; there appears to be no significant version drift from adding the workspace. The actual schema change is a real feature addition (the `showCosts` field). This should be included in the migration commit as-is.\n\n**Implication for the plan**: The plan states \"Minor diff (a few lines) from unified dependency resolution\" — the actual cause of the diff is different (it's a code change from a recently merged PR). The plan should clarify this distinction: schema diffs in the migration commit may come from either (a) dependency resolution changes after `bun install`, or (b) code changes on `develop` that affect the schema. Both are normal and should be included in the migration commit.\n\n---\n\n## Issues Found\n\nNo blocking issues. The implementation is complete and all verifiable checks pass. The only open items are:\n\n1. **Vercel configuration (Phase 7)** — This is intentionally out-of-band and requires a human to make changes in the Vercel dashboard. Not automatable by this agent. The `docs/vercel.json` is in place with the `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` flag — a human must review and confirm this flag is intentional before switching Vercel to point at the new repo location.\n\n2. **Pre-existing typecheck failure** — The `bun-types` resolution issue predates this migration and is not introduced by it. It requires a separate fix (updating `tsconfig.json` to use `@types/bun` instead of `bun-types`, or restructuring how bun-types is installed).\n\n3. **Next.js workspace root warning in local dev** — Cosmetic. Only appears in environments where the user has a `package-lock.json` higher up the directory tree. Can be silenced by adding `outputFileTracingRoot` to `docs/next.config.mjs`, but this is optional.\n\n---\n\n## Completeness Check Against Plan\n\nAll phases verified as fully implemented:\n\n| Phase | Description | Status |\n|-------|-------------|--------|\n| 0 | Preparation (branch, baseline) | Pre-work complete (baseline established) |\n| 1 | Bring docs into repo | ✅ Complete |\n| 2 | Update cross-repo references | ✅ Complete |\n| 3 | Update strip lists | ✅ Complete (all 6 steps) |\n| 4 | Update .gitignore | ✅ Complete |\n| 5 | Update documentation (SOP) | ✅ Complete (all 4 steps) |\n| 6 | Verify everything works | ✅ All verifications pass |\n| 7 | Vercel configuration | ⏳ Out-of-band, requires human action |\n| 8 | Commit, PR, and cleanup | ⏳ Pending human action |\n\n---\n\n## Notes for Plan Updates\n\n1. The warning about Next.js workspace root detection could be added as a note in Phase 1, Step 1.5 (Verify docs build locally). It's cosmetic but may confuse implementers who see it for the first time.\n\n2. The schema diff description in Phase 6, Step 6.2 and the Summary of Changes table refers to \"minor schema output diff from unified dependency resolution.\" In practice, the diff observed was from a real code change in `develop`, not dependency resolution. The plan should clarify that schema diffs can come from either source, and both are expected and normal.\n\n3. The Vercel `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` flag in `docs/vercel.json` is flagged as a human-approval gate in Phase 7, Step 7.1. The plan is correct to highlight this. No change needed.\n\n4. The release dry-run correctly fails due to uncommitted changes — this is expected and correct. The plan should note this as expected behavior when running the dry-run in the middle of the migration (before the commit in Phase 8).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":423,"cache_read_input_tokens":75917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":423},"output_tokens":2320,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b4944f-9ed8-419f-b1b0-aa5790b55960","uuid":"fb460e1c-8723-46f3-9910-4c63bfa4937c","timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:00:33.862Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WyT6QJx3oTUfB7tH8nQzjj","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/implementations/current/implementation_issues.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b4944f-9ed8-419f-b1b0-aa5790b55960","uuid":"591d2770-71b7-411c-ace5-56f906ec5706","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/implementations/current/implementation_issues.md","content":"# Implementation Issues and Observations\n\n## Overview\n\nThe implementation was already substantially complete when this agent began its review. All 8 phases from the plan were implemented and verified. This document records what was found, what was confirmed, and what observations might inform plan updates.\n\n---\n\n## State on Agent Start\n\nAll code changes were already in place as uncommitted modifications on the `develop` branch of `source/hankweave/`. The `docs/` directory was present as an untracked directory. The following files showed modifications via `git status`:\n\n- `.gitignore`\n- `bun.lock`\n- `package.json`\n- `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`\n- `scripts/generate-schemas.ts`\n- `scripts/release.ts`\n- `scripts/sync-public.ts`\n- `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`\n- `standard-operating-procedures.md`\n- `tsconfig.json`\n\nThis matched the expected change set from the plan's Summary of Changes table exactly.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Results\n\n### Linting (`bun run lint`)\n\nPassed cleanly. Biome checked 230 files with no fixes required. The changes to the scripts directory (which is excluded from Biome's `includes` per the plan's note in edge case 8) did not cause any issues.\n\n### Typecheck (`bun run tc`)\n\nFailed with the expected pre-existing error:\n\n```\nerror TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for 'bun-types'.\n```\n\nThis is the pre-existing issue documented in the plan (Phase 0, Step 0.2 and Section g). Only this single error was present — no additional errors introduced by the migration. The `docs/**/*` exclusion in `tsconfig.json` is correctly preventing docs TypeScript files from being picked up by the runtime's tsconfig.\n\n### Unit Tests (`bun run test:unit`)\n\nExact expected baseline: **1512 pass, 4 skip, 9 fail**. All 9 failures are the pre-existing Codex binary locator tests. No new failures introduced.\n\n### Integration Tests (`bun test tests/integration`)\n\n**163 pass, 0 fail**. Passed cleanly.\n\n### Schema Generation (`bun run generate-schemas`)\n\nCorrectly wrote to both:\n- `schemas/hank.schema.json`, `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`, `schemas/sentinel.schema.json`\n- `docs/public/schemas/hank.schema.json`, `docs/public/schemas/hankweave.schema.json`, `docs/public/schemas/sentinel.schema.json`\n\n### Runtime Build (`bun run build`)\n\nSucceeded. Output at `dist/index.js` (1799.54 KB minified).\n\n### Docs Build (`cd docs && bun run build`)\n\nSucceeded. Next.js compiled successfully (36 static pages). The `postbuild` Pagefind step also ran and indexed 32 pages.\n\nOne warning from Next.js was observed:\n\n```\nWarning: Next.js inferred your workspace root, but it may not be correct.\nWe detected multiple lockfiles and selected the directory of /Users/philip/package-lock.json as the root directory.\nTo silence this warning, set `outputFileTracingRoot` in your Next.js config, or consider removing one of the lockfiles if it's not needed.\nSee https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/config/next-config-js/output#caveats for more information.\nDetected additional lockfiles:\n  * /Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave/bun.lock\n```\n\nThis is a cosmetic warning from Next.js's workspace root detection heuristic on the agent's local machine — it found a `package-lock.json` higher up in the directory tree (the agent's home directory) and used that instead of the monorepo's `bun.lock`. This is an environment-specific artifact and will not appear in the actual deployment environment. The build still succeeded. **The plan could mention this potential warning in a local dev environment note.** A fix would be to set `outputFileTracingRoot` in `docs/next.config.mjs`, but this is cosmetic and not required.\n\n### npm Pack (`npm pack --dry-run`)\n\nThe tarball contains only `dist/`, `shims/`, `schemas/`, and metadata. `docs/` is correctly absent, confirming the `\"files\"` allowlist in `package.json` prevents docs from being included in the npm package.\n\n### Release Dry-Run (`bun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks`)\n\nThe release script correctly detected uncommitted changes (the migration changes not yet committed) and halted. This is correct behavior — the release script requires a clean working directory. The script showed all migration files in the uncommitted list, which is expected.\n\n---\n\n## Schema Diff Note\n\nThe plan predicted a cosmetic schema diff from unified dependency resolution. The actual schema diff found was:\n\n```diff\n+        \"showCosts\": {\n+          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n+          \"description\": \"If true, display cost data in the TUI\"\n+        },\n```\n\nThis is 4 lines added to `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`, but the change is **not from dependency resolution** — it is from the `philipn/eng-213-hankweave_runtime_show_costs` PR that was merged into `develop` before this migration. The plan's prediction about cosmetic dependency-resolution diffs was not triggered in this environment; there appears to be no significant version drift from adding the workspace. The actual schema change is a real feature addition (the `showCosts` field). This should be included in the migration commit as-is.\n\n**Implication for the plan**: The plan states \"Minor diff (a few lines) from unified dependency resolution\" — the actual cause of the diff is different (it's a code change from a recently merged PR). The plan should clarify this distinction: schema diffs in the migration commit may come from either (a) dependency resolution changes after `bun install`, or (b) code changes on `develop` that affect the schema. Both are normal and should be included in the migration commit.\n\n---\n\n## Issues Found\n\nNo blocking issues. The implementation is complete and all verifiable checks pass. The only open items are:\n\n1. **Vercel configuration (Phase 7)** — This is intentionally out-of-band and requires a human to make changes in the Vercel dashboard. Not automatable by this agent. The `docs/vercel.json` is in place with the `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` flag — a human must review and confirm this flag is intentional before switching Vercel to point at the new repo location.\n\n2. **Pre-existing typecheck failure** — The `bun-types` resolution issue predates this migration and is not introduced by it. It requires a separate fix (updating `tsconfig.json` to use `@types/bun` instead of `bun-types`, or restructuring how bun-types is installed).\n\n3. **Next.js workspace root warning in local dev** — Cosmetic. Only appears in environments where the user has a `package-lock.json` higher up the directory tree. Can be silenced by adding `outputFileTracingRoot` to `docs/next.config.mjs`, but this is optional.\n\n---\n\n## Completeness Check Against Plan\n\nAll phases verified as fully implemented:\n\n| Phase | Description | Status |\n|-------|-------------|--------|\n| 0 | Preparation (branch, baseline) | Pre-work complete (baseline established) |\n| 1 | Bring docs into repo | ✅ Complete |\n| 2 | Update cross-repo references | ✅ Complete |\n| 3 | Update strip lists | ✅ Complete (all 6 steps) |\n| 4 | Update .gitignore | ✅ Complete |\n| 5 | Update documentation (SOP) | ✅ Complete (all 4 steps) |\n| 6 | Verify everything works | ✅ All verifications pass |\n| 7 | Vercel configuration | ⏳ Out-of-band, requires human action |\n| 8 | Commit, PR, and cleanup | ⏳ Pending human action |\n\n---\n\n## Notes for Plan Updates\n\n1. The warning about Next.js workspace root detection could be added as a note in Phase 1, Step 1.5 (Verify docs build locally). It's cosmetic but may confuse implementers who see it for the first time.\n\n2. The schema diff description in Phase 6, Step 6.2 and the Summary of Changes table refers to \"minor schema output diff from unified dependency resolution.\" In practice, the diff observed was from a real code change in `develop`, not dependency resolution. The plan should clarify that schema diffs can come from either source, and both are expected and normal.\n\n3. The Vercel `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` flag in `docs/vercel.json` is flagged as a human-approval gate in Phase 7, Step 7.1. The plan is correct to highlight this. No change needed.\n\n4. The release dry-run correctly fails due to uncommitted changes — this is expected and correct. The plan should note this as expected behavior when running the dry-run in the middle of the migration (before the commit in Phase 8).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:00:34.332Z"}
